  "comments": "House of Windsor (1917 to date), Elizabeth II (1952-2022), Pre-decimal issues (1953-70).<br /><br />\r\nThe original weight of these pieces was 43.75 grains or one tenth ounce avoirdupois.<br /><br />\r\n<span style=\"font-style:italic;\">Obverse and reverse die varieties:</span><br /><br />\r\n<span style=\"font-weight:bold;\">Obverse 1</span> Cross to bead;<br />\r\n<span style=\"font-weight:bold;\">Obverse 2</span> Cross between beads;<br />\r\n<span style=\"font-weight:bold;\">Reverse A</span> F between beads;<br />\r\n<span style=\"font-weight:bold;\">Reverse B</span> F to bead;<br /><br />\r\n<a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/5a6cff358e84b.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/5a6cff358e84b.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"200\" height=\"210\" /></a><br />\r\nImage above is reproduced with kind permission of Declan Magee.<br /><br />\r\nA special mint set was released comprising 2s. 6d. to 1/4d. ordinary business strikes in transparent envelopes (1,288,000 issued).<br /><br />\r\nAlso, a special proof set was released comprising 5s. to 1/4d. struck from polished dies and sold in special cases (40,000 issued).",
